:: Meal Class Project [activity meal] {"position":"1225,2100"}
/*
{
        id: "class_project",
        passage: "Meal Class Project",
        isActive: false,
        mealType: ["breakfast", "lunch", "dinner"],
        isImportant: true,
        dayType: ["weekday", "weekend"],
        cooldown: 0,
        once: true,
        lastSeen: -1,
        present: ["mom", "sister"],
        requirements: [
        ],
        set: [
            () => setup.getMealById("class_project").isActive = false,
        ]
}
   Activated by: "Class Project" (sister_classProject). I demoed the prototype for her
   business communication presentation.
*/
<<set _cpFood to ($mealType == "breakfast" ? "cereal" : ($mealType == "lunch" ? "grilled cheese" : "spaghetti"))>>
I've barely sat down in front of my _cpFood when $sister.callName stands up, picks the salt shaker off the table and holds it up between two fingers like it's made of glass.

/* IMAGE: images/meals/important/class_project.jpg | Sister standing at the kitchen table, presenting a salt shaker like a product on stage. Mom watching with her chin in her hand, amused. */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay. Pretend this is $company.prototype.name." },
{ who: $mom, text: "That's the salt, sweetie." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Use your imagination, $mom.callName. I'm practicing. I present on Thursday and I need a test audience that won't throw things." },
{ text: "She clears her throat and puts on a voice I've never heard before, warm and slightly too slow, like a commercial for a bank." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Imagine a room that knows how you feel. Imagine a café that notices you're stressed before you do. That's $company.prototype.name. Developed right here, in a bedroom, by a man who survives exclusively on energy drinks." },
{ who: $player, text: "That's not in the script." },
{ who: $sister, text: "It's called authenticity. Professors love it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

$mom.callName is laughing, but she's also looking at me with an expression I haven't seen since high school graduation. Like I've done something she can tell her friends about.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "He really let you borrow it? For your class?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "He did a whole demo for me. It reads you, $mom.callName. Your pulse and how you're sitting and stuff. And then it just... takes the edge off. I felt amazing afterwards. Like after a spa day, except I didn't have to pay for a spa." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I know. It's very relaxing." },
{ text: "She says it before she thinks about it. Then she reaches for her glass and drinks from it for quite a long time." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Right? Everyone else is presenting phone cases. One guy is doing a water bottle. I'm going to destroy them." },
{ who: $player, text: "Just don't let anyone take it apart." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Nobody is touching my salt shaker." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She sits back down, still glowing, and spends the rest of the meal asking me questions about sensors that are better than the ones some investors asked me. I give her clean, simple answers she can put on a slide. Every one of them is true, and none of them is the important part.

When she gets up to clear her plate, she knocks her knuckles against my head on the way past. If this house had subtitles, that one would read: thanks, genius.

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 1>>
